    "Programs that paint their own 24-bit backgrounds — an agent's diff, for one — pick colours for a generic terminal. This eases them toward the palette without changing how light they are, so their text stays exactly as readable.": {
      "extractionState": "stale",
      "localizations": {
        "sv": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Program som ritar egna 24-bitarsbakgrunder, till exempel en agents diff, väljer färger för en generell terminal. Detta för dem närmare paletten utan att ändra ljusheten, så att texten förblir lika läsbar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
